<Base title="Libraries" description="Tomebound Tactics library pilot: a game whose content supply chain is real books, played in partnership with public libraries.">
  <span class="badge">In development</span>
  <h1>For libraries</h1>
  <p class="lede">Tomebound Tactics is nearly alone among mobile games: its content supply chain is real books. Players level up by studying books they hold in their hands. Libraries are not an audience for this game — they are where it is played.</p>

  <img class="hero-img" src="/library.webp" alt="A warm public library at golden hour, readers at tables and a glowing spellbook on the reading table" />

  <h2>The pilot</h2>
  <p>We are running the pilot with one Wisconsin public library at a time, for one eight-week epoch. A single partner first lets the pilot be shaped by a real library's calendar, collection, and readers before the next library is invited. Each pilot library gets:</p>
  <div class="card">
    <ul>
      <li>A canon display, curated by the library's own staff: we provide the epoch's canon shortlist, and the library selects the titles it holds or chooses to acquire, and arranges the display in its own way.</li>
      <li>A poster and QR card linking the display to the game.</li>
      <li>One optional study-night event, run by the library, in its own way.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <p>The pilot is measured without any patron data: QR-attributed signups per library, aggregate canon circulation if the library is willing to share it, total canon studies, and staff feedback. No payment either way, no exclusivity.</p>

  <h2>Privacy, stated plainly</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <ul>
      <li>No player location is collected, stored, or displayed, ever.</li>
      <li>No library-card or patron data is collected, by the game or by the library for the game.</li>
      <li>No free-text chat exists in the game.</li>
      <li>Sponsored titles are always labelled as sponsored.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <p>School libraries are out of scope for the pilot, pending a separate policy review. The pilot covers public libraries only.</p>

  <h2>Summer reading and teen programs</h2>
  <p>Epochs can align with summer reading programs and teen/YA programming: the epoch canon is a reading list, and the game rewards finishing books. Alignment is optional and shaped by each library.</p>

  <div class="card">
    <h3 style="margin-top:0">Express interest</h3>
    <p>If your library would like to be considered for the pilot, write to <strong><a href="mailto:castspells@tomeboundtactics.com">castspells@tomeboundtactics.com</a></strong>. Tell us the library, the town, and whether a canon display or a study night interests you.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
